I usually put the cursed items in a row somewhere three spaces away from
the entrance. This will keep my pet from going into the shop too far,
which will cost too much time:

   +---------+  M: me
   |SGGC.....|  P: my pet
.M.-PGGC.....|  S: shopkeeper
   |.GGC.....|  G: goodies
   +---------+  C: cursed stuff and other things I don't want

> In a food shop I don't put 10 food rations in a pile, I split
> them up into 2's and 3's.

Right. Not just because there's a bigger chance of your pet fetching at
least some food for you to use while waiting for it, but also because a
little pet cannot carry 10 of them. They're too heavy.

> I've noticed that you cannot displace you pet in, or into, a
> doorway.

Incorrect. You *can* displace your pet in, or into, a doorway.

What you cannot do is displace when you or your pet start on a shop
square (any square, not including the shop door). For example, when
you're standing in the shop doorway, you can displace a pet that is
waiting outside, but not a pet that is on the "free" shop square.

